From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:51:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Enable Enhanced Intel SpeedStep

The devicetree does not set eist_enable, so coreboot clears EIST in
IA32_MISC_ENABLE and the SSDT has no P-state tables, unlike the OEM
firmware: the OS cannot change the frequency of the processor through
ACPI, and the processor stays at its base frequency without Speed
Shift. Enable it, as the other Coffee Lake desktops do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TnH4v9ZgSCT6oudGt6KtJL
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
index 9e704b4471..c299a380a7 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@ chip soc/intel/cannonlake
 		.tdp_pl2_override = 65,
 	}"
 
+	# Enhanced Intel SpeedStep, as the OEM firmware: P-states for the OS
+	register "eist_enable" = "true"
+
 	# Unmap unused CLKREQ lines, otherwise CLKSRC #0 won't work
 	register "PcieClkSrcClkReq[1]"	= "PCIE_CLK_NOTUSED"
 	register "PcieClkSrcClkReq[5]"	= "PCIE_CLK_NOTUSED"
-- 
